WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm not asking
for any spoilers,

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I would hate to
have it spoiled,

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.204
but is it then safe to say
because of who you're married to

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:05.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
and because of where it's at
in the process,

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:08.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you know how
"Game of Thrones" ends?

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:12.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
You do know. All right.
So, just look at Camera 1.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look at Camera 1.
Don't say anything.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:17.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just think about it,
and then we'll all go back

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:18.451 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and watch this.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.587
And we're going to try to
figure out from your expression.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't say a word.
Just think about how it ends.

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:23.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is my poker face.
-Okay. Great.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:24.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are you ready?
-Yeah. Go.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:28.294
-Okay. [ Laughs ]
-Oh, my God. That was terrible.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:32.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, no.
That was a bad poker face.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:35.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's my drunk --
My drunk poker face

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:37.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
is different from
my sober poker face.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:38.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They say that's why you
probably shouldn't --

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.373 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay, grandma?!

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:41.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- I did not know
this about you.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:44.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are also a playwright.
You've written a couple plays.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.047
-Yes.
-How -- I'm fascinated by that.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:49.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm impressed by that.
What is your writing process?

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:52.619
Is there a place you like to
write more than other places?

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:56.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. It's just --
I don't have an office.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:59.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't -- I probably should
at some point,

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:00.627 size:75% position:38% line:92%
but I don't do that.

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:02.128 line:92%
And I -- It's really miserable.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:05.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Well, writing, I think,
no matter where you do it,

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:05.932 size:75% position:38% line:92%
is fairly miserable.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think there's --
Nothing's worse than

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
when people say,
"I just love to write,"

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:12.238
'cause I like to believe that
nobody actually likes to write.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:16.776
-No, the problem with me is
that when I think I finish --

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:19.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I did compare it
to childbirth,

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:22.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
because when I gave birth
to Molly, I --

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:26.252
Everyone was celebrating and
saying, "She's here, she's here.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:26.886 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The head is here."

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:30.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I breathed a
sigh of relief and was elated.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then my O.B. --
Just her head just came over

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she's like,
"Now you just got to

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:39.732 size:84% position:42% line:92%
get out the shoulders."

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Wait. What?
What are you talking about?"

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.642 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I'm not 46.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.111 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-"I am a young woman."

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:57.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sheer disbelief that it takes
another round of effort

00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:00.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you've already --
I just -- Yeah.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The rewriting,
which is, I think,

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
when the best stuff
comes out of,

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it is a drag
to have to do it, as well.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, and it's
embarrassing to look back

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:11.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
and think that I thought
that I was finished,

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:15.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, boy,
I wasn't even close.

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:17.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What a delight
to have you here.

